  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules keep the 55 °C test, per-model results to purchasers and regulators without public publication, and built-in suppression from 36 months (acceptable), while the 24-hour reporting rule (S1) is the strongest safety provision. S2 drops any sales stop above 5% (only regulator discretion, no bounded deadline), and S5 replaces the 8/100k mandatory recall with notice and regulator-discretionary recall, so no numeric recall trigger is mandatory. S3 sets new-unit shut-off at 24 months and a retrofit deadline of 72 months with an open 'where technically feasible' escape."
 },
